`PolicyEngine.load_preset()` (policy.py:441-455):
```python
path = self._dir / f"{name}.json"
if path.exists():
    try:
        data = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        return PolicySet.from_dict(data)
    except (json.JSONDecodeError, KeyError, OSError):
        logger.warning("Failed to load policy preset from %s — falling back to built-in preset '%s'", path, name, exc_info=True)
        return None
```
The log message promises a fallback the code never performs — it returns `None`, and the built-in `_STANDARD_PRESETS.get(name)` on line 455 is unreachable for that name. All three enforcement points treat `None` as "nothing to enforce": the PreToolUse hook prints `preset '<x>' not found — skipping` and returns (policy_check.py:184-192, exit 0 unless `BATON_POLICY_FAIL_CLOSED=1`); the executor's dispatch-time check does `if policy_set is None: return None` (executor.py:1685-1686); planner validation does `if policy_set is not None:` (validation.py:231-233). The pack path is equally fail-open: `register_pack_policies` is wrapped in `except Exception: pass` (policy_check.py:174-176), and an unregistered `pack:` key returns `None` (policy.py:437-439).

