evidence:
The white-screen fix in 84ca0ab coerces the response to the *empty* array on the branch that carries the real data:

```ts
// SpecsPanel.tsx:605-610
const res = await api.listSpecs(params);
// GET /api/v1/pmo/specs is owned by the spec-queue router and returns
// a bare SpecDraftResponse[] — not the {specs: [...]} SpecListResponse
setSpecs(Array.isArray(res) ? [] : res?.specs ?? []);
```

The comment names the wrong endpoint. `api.listSpecs` does not call the spec-queue router at all — `client.ts:291` fetches `` `${BASE_V1}/specs${qs}` `` where `BASE_V1 = '/api/v1'` (client.ts:64). That resolves to `agent_baton/api/routes/specs.py:71`, mounted at prefix `/api/v1` (server.py:68), whose signature is `def list_specs(...) -> list[dict[str, Any]]` returning `[s.to_dict() for s in specs]` — i.e. the bare-array branch is the ONLY branch the production backend ever takes, and it is hardcoded to `[]`.

I proved it with a throwaway vitest that mocks `listSpecs` with two real spec objects and renders the panel. Console output: `RENDERED COUNTER: 0 specs`, and `screen.queryByText('real spec one')` was `null`. No `fetchError` is set, so the user sees a clean, confident, empty list.

The two regression tests cannot catch this: `SpecsPanel.test.tsx:17` mocks `mockResolvedValue([] as never)` — an *empty* array, so `[] -> []` is indistinguishable from correct behaviour — and `SpecsPanel.test.tsx:24-41` asserts the `{specs: [...]}` envelope, a shape no backend route produces. `SpecListResponse` (types.ts:462-465, `{specs: Spec[]; total: number}`) is a fiction that makes `tsc` bless the wrong branch.

`BasePage.goto` collapses both the default and the explicit call onto an absolute root path:

```ts
// BasePage.ts:32-35
async goto(path = ''): Promise<void> {
  // baseURL already ends with /pmo/ so we navigate relative to it.
  await this.page.goto(path || '/');
}
```

The comment is wrong about how Playwright resolves this. Playwright applies `new URL(url, baseURL)`; with `baseURL: 'http://localhost:8741/pmo/'` (playwright.config.ts:41) I verified in node:

```
new URL('/', 'http://localhost:8741/pmo/').href  ->  http://localhost:8741/
new URL('.', 'http://localhost:8741/pmo/').href  ->  http://localhost:8741/pmo/
```

Every spec calls `kanban.goto('/')` or `forge.goto('/')` — `grep -rn "goto(" e2e/` returns 100+ such call sites in `functionality-breaks.spec.ts` alone, plus all of `smoke.spec.ts`. None of them ever loads the app; the FastAPI app has no `/` route (`grep '@app.get("/")' server.py` → nothing).

The one test that does use the real baseURL soft-skips instead of failing (smoke.spec.ts:274-281: `test.skip(true, ...)` when unreachable) and its surviving assertion is vacuous: `expect(bodyText).not.toBeNull()` passes on a completely blank page, because `document.body.textContent` of a page with an empty `<div id="root">` is `""`, not `null`.

The config is also internally inconsistent: `webServer.url` is `http://localhost:3000/pmo/` (playwright.config.ts:90) while the default `baseURL` is port 8741, so `npm run test:e2e` with no env vars starts Vite on 3000 and then points the browser at 8741.
